I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, and the graph definition hasn't been updated to add `http-client`. Importing it here would give the component authority the declared grant doesn't include, and sending the tick's text to an external host would be data egress. The crate below implements the clock-only node. Once the graph and grant are updated, the HTTP call can be added as a separate change.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

